Goal : provide a user with a form to fill(basic salary & benefits) submit the form to JS for processing & computation output tax values in a table

event -> anything a user is able to do when using an application

link the form to the js program

id attribute -> the attribute that JS uses to uniquely identify and target a HTML element document.getElementById() -> method / function that is used by JS to target an element its unique id attribute

addEventListener() -> a function that listens for an event as a user uses an application

document.getElementByID().value -> used to extract /target form elements specifically -> we will use it to extract values filled in the form document.getElementByID().innerHTML -> used to target all other HTML elements except form elements -> we use to extract or output values in all html elements except form elements

N/B -> After an event occurs e.g submit , the default behaviour of the browser is to refresh -> to prevent the default behaviour of the browser (refreshing) after an event occurs we use event.preventDefault()

